        "Christopher Jarzynski",
        "Denis J. Evans",
        "Giovanni Gallavotti"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The fluctuation relations give precise, broadly applicable constraints on nonequilibrium statistical physics, including systems far from equilibrium. Their conceptual reach and experimental relevance make this strong prize work.",
        "attribution": "Evans and co-workers established early fluctuation relations; Gallavotti and Cohen developed a rigorous formulation, and Jarzynski derived a powerful free-energy relation. The distinct contributions support shared credit.",
        "maturity": "The results have been tested across physical settings and remain central to modern nonequilibrium thermodynamics.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The boundaries of the discovery are broad, and the relative priority of early formulations is historically complex."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
